fixture dash_on_landing_tick_beside_step
doc docs/adr/0010, the wall (movement review 5, M4): Ash drops beside test/step's 32 u step face (x 640), 2 u from it, and would land on frame 5; an up-left dash pressed on that tick goes up-left and climbs over the step. That move lands rather than clings, so nothing turns the dash away; it used to go up-right.
room test/step
spawn 652 560
frames 30
input
  0..4
  5 L U dash
  6..29 L
end
expect
  at 5 event.dash=1 facing=-1
  never 0..29 event.wall_cling=1
  at 6 x<652u
  at 13 x<560u
end
